  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A long conducting wire having a current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> flowing through it, is bent into a circular coil of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> turns. Then it is bent into a circular coil of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> turns. The magnetic field is calculated at the centre of coils in both the cases. The ratio of the magnetic field in first case to that of second case is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GJyp9",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>n</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Ss2vX",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a1xcI",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HJAvC",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>N</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As in both cases, length of the wire will remain the same, therefore</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Now magnetic field due to single circular coil is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Therefore, required ratio of total magnetic field wil be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
